upport businesses in managing cash flow and operational efficiency. It also provides loans to small and medium-sized businesses; residential and commercial construction, and land development loans; commercial real estate loans; commercial loans; agri-business and production loans; residential mortgage loans; home equity loans and lines of credit; consumer loans; financing for marine and recreational vehicles; and small business administration and other government guaranteed loans. In addition, the company offers wealth management, consumer insurance, internet banking services, electronic bill payment services, safe deposit box rentals, telephone banking, credit and debit card services, and remote depository products, as well as access to a network of ATMs. Further, it provides health savings accounts, student savings, retirement and educational accounts, and certificates of deposit; financial advisory services; lot and small acreage loans, auto loans, working capital loans, USDA loan programs, healthcare lending, and equipment loans, as well as boat, RV, and ATV loans; agriculture lending for equipment, livestock, farmland, and crop production; homeowners, fixed life, auto, boat, renters, condo, ATV, motorcycle, and business insurance; liquidity management; and digital banking, mobile deposit, e-statements, and e-alerts services. Colony Bankcorp, Inc. was founded in 1975 and is headquartered in Fitzgerald, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. T. Heath Fountain CPA | CEO & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $879,022 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 525 people. Revenue per employee of $252K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 8%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Colony Bankcorp, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $555M market cap on $132M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +11% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $7M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.9%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 3.2% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 73% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7318302813336381},{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Colony Bankcorp (CBAN) Stock Price Ignores Q3 Earnings Strength","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/colony-bankcorp-cban-stock-price-211006256.html","date":"2026-10-30","timestamp":1793394606.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.856,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Colony Bankcorp (CBAN) Stock Price Meets Quiet Q3 Earnings Strength","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nyse-cban/colony-bankcorp/news/colony-bankcorp-cban-stock-price-meets-quiet-q3-earnings-str","date":"2026-10-29","timestamp":1793313379.873,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.925,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Colony Bankcorp (CBAN) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/colony-bankcorp-cban-q3-2026-200258000.html","date":"2026-10-29","timestamp":1793304325.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.765,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Frederick R. Saunders Reports No Holdings Upon Joining Colony Bankcorp Board","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/frederick-r-saunders-reports-no-holdings-upon-joining-colony-bankcorp-board","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793748274.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.296,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Forrest Richard Redden III Appointed to Colony Bankcorp Board, Reports No Securities Ownership","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"h